-We work in the dual triangulation $\T$ of $G$, whose triangles are coloured black and white by the two classes of $G$ (Figure~\ref{fig:cube}(b)).
-A perfect matching of $G$ is a set of edges of $\T$ containing exactly one side of every triangle, and its complement in $G$ is a single cycle exactly when this set has no cycle (Section~\ref{sec:picture}).
